//=============================================================================
// layer_desc.veryl -- E4: the layer descriptor contract and its arithmetic
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The 16 layer descriptors live in a generated ROM (gen/engine/e4_<style>.veryl,
// generated by gen/engine/e4_gen.py from gen/engine/topology.json + the frozen
// cfg/hex files).  This file is the RTL side of that contract: the field table,
// the derivations the sequencer needs, and the accounting arithmetic that the
// testbench asserts against the sequencer's own hardware counters.
//
// Field table (architecture.md 8; widths are the ROM port widths, values are
// driven straight into conv_stream/tile_reader -- nothing per-layer is
// hardcoded anywhere in the RTL):
//
//   layer_id      4   layer index inside the cascade (also the ROM index)
//   in_c          8   (7 significant bits, 1..64)  -> conv_stream.cfg_in_c
//   out_c         8   (7 significant bits, 1..64)  -> conv_stream.cfg_out_c
//   k             2   1 or 3                       -> conv_stream.cfg_k, tile_reader.cfg_k
//   stride        2   1 or 2                       -> conv_stream.cfg_stride, tile_reader
//   pad           2   0 or 1                       -> tile_reader.cfg_pad
//   relu          1   output ReLU                   -> conv_stream.cfg_relu
//   shift         6   requant right shift S         -> conv_stream.cfg_shift
//   up2x_in       1   this layer's input is nearest-2x upsampled
//   res_en        1   output sat-adds with res_pt
//   res_pt        4   point index of the residual branch (jump source)
//   res_sat       1   the add is sat_add (must be 1, architecture.md R?)
//   out_pt        4   point this layer writes
//   keep          1   the point is still referenced later in the cascade
//   unsigned_out  1   head semantics marker only (architecture.md 11 R4)
//   w_off        24   weight byte offset in the off-chip arena
//   w_bytes      24   in_c*out_c*k*k
//   b_off        24   bias int32 word offset (4 B aligned)
//   m_off        24   M0 word offset (4 B aligned)
//   x_off        24   E4 arena plan: this layer's input bytes (HWC, per layer)
//   y_off        24   E4 arena plan: this layer's output bytes (CHW, per layer)
//   x_words      24   input pixels of this layer (H*W)
//   y_bytes      24   output bytes of this layer (out_c*H_out*W_out)
//
// The arena plan fields are the one extension beyond architecture.md 8: the
// contract table fixes the *weight/bias/M0* pointers, while where a feature map
// lives is an allocator decision.  E4 makes that decision in the generated ROM
// (one flat arena per tensor class) so the sequencer can drive either dataset
// with no per-layer logic.
//
// Two feature map address conventions exist on purpose:
//   * x_off/y_off/x_words/y_bytes are BYTE counts in the HWC input / CHW output
//     layout of the cascade ledger (architecture.md 8: H/W are runtime, so the
//     byte sizes of a layer depend on the resolution -- for the layer level
//     golden run every stimulus is 16x16).  This is what an off-chip feature map
//     cache must be keyed on and what the traffic numbers in E4_ACCOUNTING.md
//     are computed from.
//   * the sequencer's feature map read port is PIXEL WORD addressed: one
//     MAXC-byte pixel word per input pixel, and in_c of those bytes are used.
//     The base is the running sum of x_words over the finished layers, which is
//     the layout the system testbench (and any on-chip pixel cache) uses.
// A real cascade can swap the read base for x_off and a byte-addressable port
// without touching the layer walk; the layer sequencing itself only needs the
// descriptor, never a per-layer constant.
//
// DSP reuse: the datapath keeps P MAC lanes and walks ceil(out_c/P) output
// channel blocks per output pixel, so the DSP cost is P + 2 (the two shared
// requant multipliers) regardless of out_c.  The whole-channel-parallel
// datapath it replaces needs ONE requant multiplier per output channel, i.e.
// 2*out_c DSP (see conv_engine.veryl / architecture.md R2) -- 128 DSP for the
// 64 channel layers, which does not fit the 93 DSPs of this board.
//=============================================================================

/// Output channel blocks a layer needs through P MAC lanes: ceil(out_c / P).






